==German==

===Etymology===
From northern {{inh|de|gmh|plat}}, {{m|gmh|blat}} and {{der|de|gml|plat}}, from {{der|de|fro|plat}}, from {{der|de|VL.|*plattus}}, probably from {{der|de|grc|πλατύς}}. Compare {{cog|nl|plat}}, {{cog|fr|plat}}, {{cog|it|piatto}}, obsolete {{cog|en|plat}}. Also related to {{cog|en|flat}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/plat/}}
* {{rhymes|de|at|s=1}}
* {{audio|de|De-platt.ogg|Audio}}

===Adjective===
{{de-adj|comp}}

# [[flat]]
# (of a building or structure; by extension also of immaterial things) completely [[destroyed]], [[razed]] to the ground
# [[bromidic]], [[banal]]
# {{lb|de|colloquial}} very [[tired]], [[exhausted]]
# {{lb|de|colloquial}} [[astonished]], [[dumbstruck]]

====Declension====
{{de-adecl|comp}}

====Synonyms====
* {{l|de|flach}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|de|Platt}}
* {{l|de|Plattfuß}}
* {{l|de|Platter}}
* {{l|de|Plattbauchspinne}}

